# .trivyignore — accepted/deferred vulnerabilities
#
# ── 2026-11-07 update ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CI gate (trivy fs, severity=CRITICAL,HIGH, ignore-unfixed) started
# failing because new CVEs landed against the dependency versions pinned by
# Spring Boot 3.2.12. Instead of ignoring all of them, the ones that live on
# a release line we already use were FIXED in pom.xml via patch-level
# property overrides (same major/minor line as the version Boot 3.2.12 was
# tested against, so no framework upgrade):
#
#   jackson-bom.version 2.15.4        -> 2.18.11     (5 CVEs, Jackson 2.x)
#   tomcat.version      10.1.33       -> 10.1.61     (6 CVEs, Tomcat 10.1.x)
#   netty.version       4.1.115.Final -> 4.1.137.Final (1 CVE, Netty 4.1.x)
#
# Dead entries for those fixes were pruned from this file on purpose: if any
# of them regresses, the gate MUST fail again.
#
# What is left is the set of findings whose only fix ships with Spring
# Framework 6.2/7.0, Spring Security 6.5+, Spring Boot 3.3+/3.5/4.0 and
# Micrometer 1.15+. Those cannot be reached from Spring Boot 3.2.x, which is
# EOL and will never receive them.
#
# Decision: defer to the dedicated Spring Boot 3.4/3.5 (or 4.x) upgrade
# sprint — see docs/history/optimalisasi-v3/06-final-report-phaseV3-5.md.
# The gate stays ENABLED: any NEW CVE not listed below fails the build, and
# every entry here must be removed as the upgrade lands.
#
# ── Remaining deferred findings (11) ─────────────────────────────────────
# spring-webmvc/spring-core/spring-expression 6.1.15 -> 6.2.19 / 7.0.9
CVE-2025-41249
CVE-2026-41842
CVE-2026-41845
CVE-2026-41850
CVE-2026-47884
# spring-security-crypto/spring-security-web 6.2.8 -> 6.2.10 / 6.5.9
CVE-2025-22228
CVE-2026-22732
# spring-boot / spring-boot-starter-actuator 3.2.12 -> 3.3.11 / 3.5.12
CVE-2025-22235
CVE-2026-22733
# micrometer-core 1.12.13 -> 1.15.12
CVE-2026-40984
# postgresql 42.6.2 -> 42.7.11 (maintenance release; bundle with the upgrade
# sprint so the JDBC driver is validated together with the rest)
CVE-2026-42198
